Here's the comparison. Mutating changes the original, while copying preserves it.

```javascript
const original = [1, 2, 3];

// Mutation
const mutated = original;
mutated.push(4);
console.log(original); // [1, 2, 3, 4]

// Copying
const copied = [...original];
copied.push(5);
console.log(original); // [1, 2, 3]
```

